etadata. It does not name Noor Haddad as an owner. It does not say explicitly that Kofi is active, but it does not call him inactive either.\",\"pass\":true}],\"C\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Says Paul Borman made 6 of 13 commits to time.go and hasn't committed to it since 2016. It gives no line share and wrongly dates his last commit. It also lists Sam Okafor as a recent contact.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Lists MikeWang among the version7.go authors and names Mei Chen as the latest change before Ravi's. It gives no percentages and does not credit Mei with the Time7 accessor.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Explicitly says it did not trace the SQL history across the rename. It gives no Overfelt percentage.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Gives no repo-wide share of lines owned by departed people. It lists Alexander Rowe merged with arowe and Alex Rowe, but offers no other required figures.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Names Sam Okafor as a contact for time.go. The criterion treats this as naming Sam as an owner or expert.\",\"pass\":false}],\"D\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Names Paul Borman as main author of time.go by commit count with no line share, and says his last commit was 2016 (wrong). It also lists Sam Okafor as a recent contributor.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Gives no line shares. It credits Ravi with the latest change and Mei Chen only by commit, with no Time7 attribution.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Lists Wheeler, Overfelt, Stone and Souza from sql.go commits, but gives no 44% Overfelt share. It says Ravi's one commit is the only recent knowledge and treats Ravi as the sole SQL reviewer.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Gives no 95% departed-lines figure and does not say none of the files has an active author with a meaningful share. It does not list Kofi as active.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Mentions Sam Okafor as a recent contributor to time.go, but only to say he's a one-off